    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Earth rotates 360° in 24 hours, which translates to 15° per hour or 1° every 4 minutes.",
        "Latitude measures distance North or South of the Equator (0°), while Longitude measures distance East or West of the Prime Meridian (0°).",
        "Indian Standard Time (IST) is based on the 82°30' E longitude, passing near Prayagraj / Mirzapur.",
        "Time increases as you travel East from the Prime Meridian (+ GMT) and decreases as you travel West (- GMT).",
        "The International Date Line lies near the 180° meridian; crossing it eastward gains a day, while crossing westward loses a day."
      ],
      "id": "2rm48hd"
    },
